answers:
I think in *ngFor you didn't use the trackBy function before, right? In angular 17 when you use @for you have to set the track function which is the same as the trackBy function in the old angular version. In your code I see you set it to track $index which means angular always thinks it's still the same element and never changes. To resolve this problem, you should change the track function to something like track activeProblem.
As example:
 @for (activeProblem of summary.activeProblems; track activeProblem) {
      <app-active-problem class="panel" [activeProblem] = "activeProblem" (update)="updateActiveProblem($event);"></app-active-problem>
 }

